\chapter{System Design}

The purpose of this chapter is to provide information that is complementary
to the code of the MazdoorLink platform. Without an adequate design that
delivers the required functions as well as quality attributes, the project
will fail. Communicating architecture to its stakeholders is as important a
job as creating it in the first place. This chapter presents the structural
and behavioral design artifacts of the MazdoorLink system, including the
software architecture, class diagram, sequence diagrams, entity relationship
diagram, database schema, user interface design, and a list of third-party
software components used in the development of the system.

Two views are considered while defining the software architecture of the
MazdoorLink platform. The structural view encompasses the architecture
diagram, component diagram, and class diagram, which collectively describe
the static organization of the system. The behavioral view encompasses the
sequence diagrams and activity diagrams, which describe the dynamic
interactions and workflows within the system. Both views together provide a
comprehensive understanding of the system design.

The MazdoorLink platform follows a \textbf{Serverless Client-Side
Architecture} as its primary architectural style. A Flutter mobile frontend
communicates directly with Firebase services (Authentication and Firestore)
and external APIs (Cloudinary and Google Maps Platform) without any
intermediate application server or custom backend. All business logic that
requires real-time data operates through Firestore snapshot streams and
client-side processing within the Flutter application. The
\textbf{Repository Pattern} is applied in the service layer to abstract
Firestore operations from the UI logic through dedicated service classes
such as \texttt{workers\_service.dart} and \texttt{cloudinary\_service.dart}.
The \textbf{Observer Pattern} is realized through Firestore real-time
listeners, which propagate live data updates directly to the Flutter widgets
without any polling mechanism.

