\section{Sequence Diagrams}

Sequence diagrams, when used in conjunction with class diagrams, provide an
extremely effective communication mechanism for the MazdoorLink system.
UML sequence diagrams illustrate how objects interact in a given situation
by showing the messages sent among the instances of these classes and the
order in which they are sent. The following sequence diagrams describe the
key interaction flows within the MazdoorLink platform.

Because MazdoorLink follows a serverless client-side architecture, all
sequence diagrams show the Flutter client communicating directly with
Firebase Authentication, Cloud Firestore, and Cloudinary. There is no
intermediate application server or Cloud Function in any interaction flow.
The Firestore real-time snapshot stream is the primary mechanism through
which status changes and new data are propagated to all listening clients
without any polling.

