\subsection*{Sequence Diagram 1: Customer Login and Registration}

Figure~\ref{fig:sd01} illustrates the sequence of interactions that occur
when a customer registers or logs in to the MazdoorLink platform using
OTP-based phone number verification. The customer submits a phone number
through the Flutter application, which forwards the request directly to
Firebase Authentication. Firebase Auth dispatches an OTP to the customer's
mobile number and, upon successful verification, issues a JWT session token
with a unique \texttt{uid}. The Flutter client then checks whether a
\texttt{users} document with that \texttt{uid} already exists in Firestore.
If no document is found, the client writes a new one with
\texttt{role: customer} and navigates the user to the home screen. If the
document already exists, the session is resumed and the customer is
navigated directly to the home screen.

