\subsection*{Sequence Diagram 2: Customer Posts Job Request}

Figure~\ref{fig:sd02} illustrates the sequence of interactions that occur
when a customer posts a job request. The customer selects a service
category and specific issues through the Flutter application, which then
queries Firestore directly for all \texttt{users} documents where
\texttt{role = worker}, \texttt{status = approved}, the category matches,
and \texttt{isOnline = true}. The Flutter client applies a client-side
skill-intersection filter against the returned worker documents to retain
only those whose \texttt{skills} array contains the selected issues. The
customer reviews the filtered worker list, selects a worker, specifies a
price and payment method, and taps ``Hire''. The Flutter client writes a
new document to the Firestore \texttt{jobs} collection with
\texttt{status: pending} and an \texttt{expiresAt} timestamp. The selected
worker's \texttt{streamWorkerJobs} listener detects the new document and
surfaces the job offer on the worker's dashboard in real time.

