``Accept''. The Flutter client updates the \texttt{status} field of the
job document in Firestore directly to \texttt{accepted}. The customer's
own job stream listener detects this status change in real time and
updates the customer's dashboard to reflect that the worker has accepted
and is on the way. The chat channel between the two parties becomes active
once the job reaches the \texttt{accepted} state.

