\section{Database Schema}

The database schema of the MazdoorLink platform defines the logical
structure of all data stored within Cloud Firestore. Firestore organizes
data as collections of documents, where each document contains key-value
pairs representing the attributes of a data entity. The schema described
in this section defines the primary Firestore collections, their document
field structures, field types, and the relationships maintained through
stored \texttt{uid} references.

The \textbf{users} collection is the single collection that stores profile
documents for all registered users of the platform, regardless of role.
Each user document is identified by the \texttt{uid} assigned by Firebase
Authentication and contains the following fields: \texttt{uid} (string,
primary identifier), \texttt{role} (string, one of \texttt{customer},
\texttt{worker}, or \texttt{admin}), \texttt{name} (string),
\texttt{phone} (string), \texttt{profileImageUrl} (string, Cloudinary
URL), and \texttt{status} (string, one of \texttt{active},
\texttt{suspended}, or \texttt{banned}). Documents belonging to workers
carry additional fields: \texttt{serviceCategory} (string),
\texttt{cnicImageUrl} (string, Cloudinary URL),
\texttt{verificationStatus} (string, one of \texttt{pending},
\texttt{approved}, or \texttt{rejected}), \texttt{isOnline} (boolean),
\texttt{lastSeenAt} (timestamp), and \texttt{skills} (array of maps,
each map containing \texttt{skillName} (string) and \texttt{rate}
(number)).

The \textbf{jobs} collection acts as the transactional ledger of the
platform. Each document contains: \texttt{jobId} (string),
\texttt{customerId} (string, reference to \texttt{users}),
\texttt{workerId} (string, reference to \texttt{users}),
\texttt{serviceCategory} (string), \texttt{selectedIssues} (array of
strings), \texttt{price} (number), \texttt{paymentMethod} (string),
\texttt{locationCoordinates} (geopoint), \texttt{status} (string, one
of \texttt{pending}, \texttt{accepted}, \texttt{working},
\texttt{completed}, \texttt{declined}, \texttt{cancelled}, or
\texttt{expired}), \texttt{createdAt} (timestamp), and
\texttt{expiresAt} (timestamp).

The \textbf{conversations} collection powers the real-time chat feature.
Each document contains: \texttt{conversationId} (string),
\texttt{jobId} (string, reference to \texttt{jobs}),
\texttt{customerId} (string), \texttt{workerId} (string), and
\texttt{createdAt} (timestamp). Each conversation document contains a
\textbf{messages} subcollection where individual message documents are
stored with the fields: \texttt{messageId} (string), \texttt{senderId}
(string), \texttt{content} (string), and \texttt{timestamp} (timestamp).

The \textbf{complaints} collection stores complaint records submitted by
customers. Each document contains: \texttt{complaintId} (string),
\texttt{customerId} (string), \texttt{workerId} (string),
\texttt{jobId} (string), \texttt{description} (string),
\texttt{evidenceUrls} (array of Cloudinary URL strings), and
\texttt{status} (string, one of \texttt{open}, \texttt{underReview},
\texttt{resolved}, or \texttt{rejected}).

The \textbf{damage\_claims} collection stores formal damage claim records
reviewed by administrators. Each document contains:
\texttt{claimId} (string), \texttt{complaintId} (string, reference to
\texttt{complaints}), \texttt{workerId} (string), \texttt{customerId}
(string), \texttt{adminDecision} (string), \texttt{deductionAmount}
(number), and \texttt{resolvedAt} (timestamp).

