\section{User Interface Design}

User Interface (UI) design for the MazdoorLink platform focuses on
anticipating what each category of user needs to accomplish and ensuring
that the interface provides elements that are easy to access, understand,
and use to facilitate those actions. The UI design brings together concepts
from interaction design, visual design, and information architecture. The
design philosophy of the MazdoorLink platform is guided by two primary
principles: simplicity for low-literacy workers and comprehensiveness for
technically proficient customers and administrators.

The customer-facing interface follows a clean, card-based material design
language with clear visual hierarchy, intuitive navigation through a
bottom navigation bar, and prominent call-to-action buttons. The
worker-facing interface is intentionally simplified, featuring large
one-tap action buttons, high-contrast colors, Urdu as the default language,
and a prominent availability toggle for presence management. The
administrator interface provides a data-dense dashboard with list views,
status badges, and action buttons for managing users, verifying documents,
and resolving complaints. All interfaces share a consistent global design
system defined in \texttt{app\_theme.dart}, which provides color palettes
(teals, reds, amber), typography, and standard widget styles throughout
the application to ensure visual coherence.

