\subsection*{UI Screen 5: Job Tracking and Active Booking Screen}

Once a worker accepts an incoming service request, both the customer and
the worker transition to a synchronized, real-time job tracking interface
designed to coordinate the active booking. The screen displays a prominent
visual progress tracker showing the current booking state, such as Worker
En Route, Job in Progress, or Completed.

The interface also shows basic provider and client details, including
names, contact shortcuts, and the selected service category so both
parties can verify the active task. Quick-access utilities allow the user
to open real-time chat or launch voice-guided navigation and assistance
for coordinating arrival at the job location. High-contrast lifecycle
buttons allow the parties to verify job commencement and mark the task as
complete once the service has been successfully delivered.

